%description:
Tests a client that gets an AccECN SYN-ACK after its fallback SYN (RFC 9768
section 3.1.4.1): it "enters the feedback mode appropriate to the first SYN/ACK
it receives according to Table 2". The tester removes the third SYN (no ECN
flags) and the SYN-ACKs except B002, which it delays until after that SYN. The
client uses AccECN and sets ECT ("it is still allowed to set ECT"), but the
server, which sent SYN-ACKs with (0,0,0), sends Not-ECT data (section 3.1.5).

%inifile: omnetpp.ini
[General]
record-vector-results = false
ned-path = .;../../../../src;../../lib

cmdenv-event-banners=false
cmdenv-express-mode=false

*.testing=true
cmdenv-log-prefix="[%c]: "

*.cli_app.sendScript="12.0 1000"
*.srv_app.sendScript="13.0 1000"
*.*_tcp.tcpEcnMode = "accecn"
*.tcptester.script="a3 delete; b1 delete; b2 delay 7; b3 delete; b4 delete"

include ../../lib/defaults.ini

%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%file: postrun.pl
open FILE, '<test.out';
while($sor = <FILE>)
{
    if ($sor =~ /^\[testing\]: (.*)$/)
    {
        print "$1\n";
    }
}
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%postrun-command:  perl ./postrun.pl
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%contains: postrun-command(1).out
[9.001 A003] A.1000 > B.2000: S 0:0(0) win 16384   Option(s): MaxSegSize# deleting
[9.003 B004] A.1000 < B.2000: A S 500:500(0) ack 1 win 16384   Option(s): MaxSegSize# deleting
[10.003 B004] A.1000 < B.2000: A S W 500:500(0) ack 1 win 16384   Option(s): MaxSegSize# introducing copy
cli_tcp: SYN_SENT --> ESTABLISHED  (on RCV_SYN_ACK)
[10.005 A004] A.1000 > B.2000: A W ack 501 win 16384   Option(s): NOP AccECN0(e0b=1,ceb=0,e1b=1)
srv_tcp: SYN_RCVD --> ESTABLISHED  (on RCV_ACK)
[12.001 A005] A.1000 > B.2000: A E N 1:1001(1000) ack 501 win 16384 ECT(0)   Option(s): NOP AccECN0(e0b=1,ceb=0,e1b=1)
[12.203 B005] A.1000 < B.2000: A E N ack 1001 win 16384   Option(s): NOP NOP NOP AccECN0(e0b=1001)
[13.001 B006] A.1000 < B.2000: A E N 501:1501(1000) ack 1001 win 16384 
[13.203 A006] A.1000 > B.2000: A E N ack 1501 win 16384 
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%postrun-command: grep "undisposed object:" test.out > test_undisposed.out || true
%not-contains: test_undisposed.out
undisposed object: (
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
